<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cenepa War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1995</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cenepa War was a short conflict between Ecuador and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> fought in January and February 1995 over outposts in the upper Cenepa valley, in an undemarcated stretch of the Cordillera del Cóndor. Ecuadorian forces held most of their positions, and a ceasefire was agreed under the guarantors of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-protocol">Rio de Janeiro Protocol</a>. Negotiations led to the final border settlement of 1998.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cenepa-war.jpg" alt="Cenepa War" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The University of Texas at Austin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cenepa_river_basin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
